WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:04.510
BETH: Supporting individuals with
autism to take positive risks in their

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:08.730
lives is not about encouraging them
to do dangerous activities or things.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:13.449
It’s about getting them to take control
of their lives and make choices and then

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.409
learn from the consequences of those
choices whether positive or negative.

00:00:18.219 --> 00:00:21.880
Everyone has the right to take risks,
no matter how scary it might be,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.950
especially for those supporting them.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.290
However, there is still a need for
‘safeguarding’ or ‘duty of care’

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.259
with all risks that may be taken.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:35.700
JOE: Risk is a necessary and important
part of life for everyone, but we need

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.830
to think about how risk affects those
with autism and manage this risk.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.910
When managing risk, there is the potential
for carers to be overcautious and

00:00:44.929 --> 00:00:49.520
overprotective of an individual, depending
on the severity of their disorder.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:53.250
BETH: By identifying the risks
associated with an activity for an

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:57.660
individual and assessing how that
activity can be completed effectively

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.020
and safely, can help them to build
confidence and develop new skills.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:06.399
Also understanding that there are
consequences to taking risks both

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:11.019
positive and negative, can help to promote
the ability to learn from mistakes.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.270
JOE: Carers can empower the individual
to have a more fulfilling life through

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:20.140
positive risk-taking, and this can
bring real benefits, when it takes into

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.300
account the needs and preferences of
the individual and their circumstances.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.840
The individual is then enabled to grow
in confidence, learning from their

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:33.270
experiences, and developing new skills
and abilities, and make full use of

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.020
their opportunities and potential.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.330
BETH: Supporting individuals with
autism to take positive risks puts them

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.269
more in control of their own lives.

00:01:41.789 --> 00:01:45.940
Risk shouldn’t be seen as a negative
experience that’s best avoided as

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:49.300
this can lead to an individual having
a more limited life experience.

